/* MSG — The Long Aftertaste: the long radio call. 20 chapters of original 2037 fiction and a sourced
   history of MSG. Each line is [speaker, text, source ids, chapter index]. Research checked: 7 September 2026. */
export default {"chapters":[{"title":"THE WRONG WAR","subtitle":"Transfer complete · 2037","start":0,"end":8,"words":397},{"title":"BEFORE THE CRYSTAL","subtitle":"Ancient food traditions · 1866","start":8,"end":16,"words":427},{"title":"A BOWL IN TOKYO","subtitle":"1908 · Kikunae Ikeda","start":16,"end":24,"words":428},{"title":"SELLING THE FIFTH TASTE","subtitle":"1909 · Ajinomoto begins","start":24,"end":32,"words":410},{"title":"THE MAP UNDER THE LABEL","subtitle":"1910–1946 · Factories and routes","start":32,"end":40,"words":417},{"title":"A FACTORY THAT BREATHES","subtitle":"1956 · Fermentation changes the scale","start":40,"end":48,"words":376},{"title":"FROM SUGAR TO CRYSTAL","subtitle":"A production line, not a spell","start":48,"end":56,"words":409},{"title":"TWO SIGNALS, ONE TASTE","subtitle":"1913–2002 · Umami is not one ingredient","start":56,"end":64,"words":422},{"title":"THE LETTER","subtitle":"1968 · A question becomes a reputation","start":64,"end":72,"words":412},{"title":"THE RUMOR THAT LEARNED TO WALK","subtitle":"Stigma, evidence, and the edited record","start":72,"end":80,"words":437},{"title":"DOSE AND DOCUMENTS","subtitle":"1995–2017 · Safety is not a slogan","start":80,"end":88,"words":422},{"title":"A LABEL IS NOT A MOLECULE","subtitle":"Names, ingredients, and the missing context","start":88,"end":96,"words":393},{"title":"MORE THAN A BOTTLE","subtitle":"Ajinomoto as an industrial case study","start":96,"end":104,"words":406},{"title":"THE FILM INSIDE THE MACHINE","subtitle":"1999 · Ajinomoto Build-up Film","start":104,"end":112,"words":454},{"title":"WHO OWNS THE EXPLANATION","subtitle":"The 2020s · The story remains contested","start":112,"end":120,"words":403},{"title":"MONOSODIUM GOVERNANCE","subtitle":"2037 · Project PANTRY · Fiction","start":120,"end":128,"words":396},{"title":"THE WOMAN AT TABLE FOUR","subtitle":"Mara's record · Fiction","start":128,"end":139,"words":419},{"title":"THE UNIT THAT COULD NOT GO HOME","subtitle":"Rook's record · Fiction","start":139,"end":148,"words":451},{"title":"THE SECOND TRANSFER","subtitle":"Copy evidence. Release the hold. · Fiction","start":148,"end":156,"words":376},{"title":"DESSERT","subtitle":"One more thing · Fiction","start":156,"end":166,"words":359}],"lines":[["MARA","Rook. Do not leave that room. The download is complete, but the file is not a weapons plan. It is a food ledger. Four hundred pages of invoices. Fermentation equipment. Freight insurance. School meals. At the center of every route are the same three letters: MSG. Not a callsign. Not a missile system. Monosodium glutamate. You crossed a frozen dock to recover the history of a seasoning.","",0],["ROOK","I put six armed men between myself and a bag of flavor. Control, check the file again. There has to be a warhead under the soup. They do not put a security camera above a noodle recipe unless the noodle recipe has a launch code.","",0],["MARA","I checked it three times. That is the trap. They wanted us to look for a weapon in the powder. The powder is ordinary food-grade MSG. The weapon is the system that decides who may receive the next shipment. We have been following the wrong kind of chain. Not a chain of command. A supply chain.","",0],["ROOK","Then tell me who owns the chain. Keep it short. There is a patrol on the other side of the wall, and the chair in this room was designed by a man who hated the human spine.","",0],["MARA","I cannot explain the contract without the industry. I cannot explain the industry without the taste. And I cannot explain the taste without returning to a kitchen more than a century ago. This channel has enough storage. The guards and mission clock are paused while we talk. Settle in, Rook. We are going to discuss the whole archive. There are chapter controls. Use them with dignity.","",0],["ROOK","You paused the operation for a lecture? I thought our radio had a burst mode. A burst is supposed to be brief. That is what makes it a burst instead of a siege.","",0],["MARA","Before we begin, one boundary matters. The historical people, companies, and research in this archive are real. Frostline, Palisade Logistics, Project PANTRY, and our operation are fiction. Ajinomoto and the other real producers are not the secret enemy. Their public history is the evidence we use to understand our invented enemy. The source buttons separate the two. Do not mistake the plot for a food warning.","",0],["ROOK","Understood. Real seasoning. Fictional conspiracy. Very real cold feet. Start at the beginning, and when you reach the end, resist the urge to reveal a second beginning.","",0],["MARA","People knew savory food long before anyone named umami. Fermented sauces, aged cheese, and stocks could supply glutamate. The important distinction is between a taste people used and a substance scientists later identified. Cooks did not need a structural formula to notice that a broth had depth. MSG as a manufactured seasoning came much later. Its history did not create the older food traditions from which it learned.","S01",1],["ROOK","So the taste was already in the kitchen. It did not arrive with an industrial drum and a guard detail. That makes our target less like a new weapon and more like an old road someone decided to put a tollbooth across.","",1],["MARA","In 1866, the German chemist Karl Heinrich Ritthausen identified glutamic acid after treating wheat gluten. That is the chemical milestone. It is not the date when MSG seasoning went on sale. Glutamic acid, the acid; glutamate, its related ionic form; and monosodium glutamate, a sodium salt, are connected terms, not three separate inventions of flavor. Keep the names distinct, or the timeline starts to lie.","S02",1],["ROOK","Eighteen sixty-six. I have been on the radio for two minutes, and we are already farther from extraction than when I stepped off the boat. Does the file contain a shortcut through the nineteenth century?","",1],["MARA","No. The nineteenth century has no ventilation shaft. Listen to what the distinction does to the case. Our enemy titled its first report DISCOVERY OF THE HUNGER SWITCH. But identifying a substance is not discovering a switch. That title turned a laboratory observation into a promise of control. It was the first false step in their sales presentation. Every slide after it walked in the same direction.","",1],["ROOK","My old unit called the kitchen the rear area. Nothing important was supposed to happen there. Yet every order depended on the truck reaching it. We could lose a radio for a day. Lose the cook for a day, and suddenly every officer remembered that soldiers were animals with schedules.","",1],["MARA","The ledger understands that better than your officers did. It contains no superhuman chemistry. It contains meal times. Delivery windows. Names at tables. A map can hide a person inside a symbol. This map hides a person inside an average daily demand. That is why I need you to see the ordinary history first. Otherwise every ordinary fact in the room will look like a miracle.","",1],["ROOK","All right. Before the crystal there was food. Before the food ledger there were people. I will try to remember that when the next chapter tries to convince me the soup is in command.","",1],["MARA","In 1908, Kikunae Ikeda at Tokyo Imperial University identified glutamate as the source of the distinct savory taste in kombu broth. He called the taste umami. Sweet, sour, salty, and bitter did not fully describe what he found. He was not inventing seaweed soup. He was isolating and naming one of its taste components. A familiar meal became a precise research question.","S03",2],["ROOK","He looked at dinner and asked why it worked. My commanding officer looked at dinner and asked why we were still sitting down. The professor had the better method. What happened between the broth and the powder?","",2],["MARA","Ikeda investigated salts of glutamic acid and developed MSG as a usable seasoning. Combining glutamate with sodium gave a practical product. His paper on new seasonings appeared in 1909. An English translation was published in Chemical Senses in 2002. Those dates refer to different events: discovery, publication, and later translation. A date on an archive copy is not always the date of the work inside it.","S04",2],["ROOK","A document can be older than its cover. That explains the report on the terminal. The server says it was created last month, but the photographs show equipment we stopped using before I joined. Someone did not invent a new program. Someone put a new cover on an old one.","",2],["MARA","Yes. Their archive is full of that move. A familiar thing gets a new name, then a higher classification. A dinner becomes a sensory event. A warehouse becomes a nutritional control site. A missed delivery becomes a population response. Nothing in the room changes except the words above the door. But once the words change, different people believe they are allowed to give the orders.","",2],["ROOK","I can see a bowl beside the keyboard. White, with a blue line around the rim. There is a spoon in it. You could put this room inside a school kitchen if you removed the rifle rack. Maybe that is the part I dislike. It is not alien enough to be comfortable.","",2],["MARA","Remember the bowl. We will come back to it. Not because it contains a secret. Because the people who built this place wanted us to forget that bowls are made to be filled. They preferred their diagrams empty. An empty bowl was a demand signal. A full bowl was a cost. The distinction made perfect sense to a system that never had to eat.","",2],["ROOK","There it is. The first line I will hear in my sleep. Continue, Control. I assume the professor does not turn out to be my father. We are already carrying enough dates.","",2],["MARA","Ikeda worked with the entrepreneur Saburosuke Suzuki II. The business launched AJI-NO-MOTO seasoning in 1909. The brand name is often rendered as essence of taste. Ajinomoto's account links the founders' project to an aim of better food and nutrition. That is the manufacturer's own account of its origins. It helps explain its identity, but a company history is also a company speaking about itself.","S05 S19",3],["ROOK","A chemist and an entrepreneur. One person finds the taste. The other finds a bottle, a factory, and someone willing to pay. I assume that is where the story becomes less pure. Every mission does, when it reaches the purchase order.","",3],["MARA","The commercial process was not simply to boil endless vats of kombu. Early glutamate production used protein hydrolysis, notably from wheat gluten. Hydrolysis breaks proteins down so their components can be recovered. The starting material and process mattered to cost and scale. A discovery in seaweed broth could therefore become an industrial product through a different raw material. That change did not make the history of the broth false.","S06",3],["ROOK","The enemy briefing makes every change in production sound like contamination. Original process good. New process suspicious. As though a spoonful could become hostile because its paperwork had a different supplier.","",3],["MARA","That is how Palisade sells fear in our case. The brochure has two columns. OLD is warm, safe, and expensive. NEW is cold, dangerous, and somehow available only through a Palisade-certified distributor. The third column is missing. It should say WHO TESTED IT. They replaced evidence with a lighting choice. Then they charged a fee to move a product from one photograph to the other.","",3],["ROOK","I used to sign for crates without opening them. The form had three boxes: received, damaged, missing. No box for WHY IS THIS HERE. I suppose that is how a factory becomes invisible. Everything arrives in pieces small enough for one person to approve.","",3],["MARA","We should not replace their propaganda with a heroic advertisement. Businesses need workers, resources, customers, and public trust. They make useful things and have interests of their own. Our real manufacturer belongs in that complicated world. The fictional contractor took a different step. It decided trust could be rented, and that every meal should stop working when the rent was late.","",3],["ROOK","Put that sentence beside the bottle, not on it. A label should tell me what the product is. It should not need forty minutes to explain which part of my freedom is a recurring service.","",3],["MARA","Ajinomoto's timeline records distribution in Taiwan and Korea in 1910, a Kawasaki factory in 1914, and S. Suzuki & Co. Ltd. in 1917. It also records a New York office in 1917 and a Shanghai office in 1918. Product launch in 1909 and corporate establishment in 1917 are different milestones. That is why brief summaries can give different starting dates without describing the same event.","S07",4],["MARA","The timeline records destruction of its head office and Kawasaki factory in the 1923 Great Kanto Earthquake. It lists the name Ajinomoto Honpo S. Suzuki & Co., Ltd. in 1932, and Ajinomoto Co., Inc. in 1946. This is not a smooth line from discovery to success. Buildings, offices, and names changed. A bag on a shelf can conceal decades of work and disruption.","S07",4],["ROOK","The map on my screen has no buildings. Just arrows. Nothing burns down on an arrow. Nobody misses a shift. Nobody waits for a train that no longer runs. Whoever drew this has removed every event that might make the customer ask who carried the load.","",4],["MARA","Exactly. We can describe an expansion without making it a victory parade. The archive's dates sit inside wider histories of empire, war, disaster, trade, and rebuilding. This call is a route through the MSG story, not every person's complete history. When a company timeline gives only an opening date, it does not give us permission to invent the lives behind that opening. Absence in the record is not proof of innocence or guilt.","",4],["ROOK","That is inconvenient for a man who gets paid to identify the villain before the loading screen ends. The office across the dock had one photograph. A child beside a bicycle. I turned it face down before I took the keycard. I did not want the guard to have a life while I was using his desk as cover.","",4],["MARA","Turn it back up on your way out. The contractor's system will call that an unnecessary action. I am adding it to your orders anyway. You do not have to know the person in a photograph to understand why it should face the room.","",4],["ROOK","There is no score bonus for that, is there? No medal. No radio message telling me I performed a humanitarian desk correction. Just a photograph where its owner left it.","",4],["MARA","Correct. The history is full of things that matter without becoming a statistic. That is one of the reasons this transmission is so long. I am trying to return the missing nouns to a document made entirely of numbers.","",4],["MARA","The next major production change was fermentation. Kyowa Hakko's history credits its researchers with a glutamic-acid fermentation process in 1956. This achievement should not be assigned to Ajinomoto simply because that is the better-known MSG brand. The industrial history contains more than one company. A famous name is not a substitute for tracing who did which work.","S08",5],["MARA","Research histories link this change to Corynebacterium glutamicum, a bacterium used to produce glutamate. The process enabled much larger, lower-cost output and helped expand amino-acid fermentation beyond glutamate. Think of a controlled biological production system, not a machine that mines finished crystals from a plant. The organism makes the product under conditions selected by the producer.","S09",5],["ROOK","A living factory. Something small enough to miss without a microscope, doing work large enough to change a freight map. My file called it a bio-reactive agent. I expected a containment suit. It turns out the dramatic name was doing most of the fighting.","",5],["MARA","The file uses the same red triangle for a fermentation tank, a rifle magazine, and a leaking roof. All three are classified as operational risk. After enough red triangles, the reader stops asking which kind. That is the first thing Palisade automated. Not a factory. A failure to make distinctions.","",5],["ROOK","Could they control the bacteria to control the people? Before you answer, understand that this is the question a field agent asks when the radio has already covered half a chemistry degree.","",5],["MARA","No hidden obedience function follows from those facts. Our plot does not give MSG one. The company in this story controls access, not the molecules in a person's thoughts. A kitchen can have good ingredients and still be locked. A truck can carry safe food and still be sent to the wrong place. The threat is the decision attached to the shipment.","",5],["ROOK","Then the tanks on this map are not secret weapons. They are evidence that the world knows how to make the thing. The shortage they sold us was not inevitable. Someone chose where the trucks would stop.","",5],["MARA","You have it. Do not let the word biological turn a useful industrial process into a monster. We have enough real decisions to investigate. We do not need to invent a chemical crime to make the room interesting.","",5],["MARA","Modern MSG production commonly starts with plant-derived carbohydrate sources. Producers use fermentation, then separate, purify, and crystallize the product. Ajinomoto describes feedstocks such as sugarcane and cassava. The familiar white seasoning is not the whole fermented broth poured into a shaker. There are recovery and purification steps between the tank and the finished material.","S10",6],["MARA","This is one reason a feedstock is not a complete description of the final ingredient. A process changes material. The useful questions concern the identified product, its specifications, the manufacturing controls, and how it is used. Naming a raw material does not replace those questions. Nor does the word natural answer all of them.","S10",6],["ROOK","There is a bag beside the terminal. The label says FOOD GRADE. Under it, someone stamped NOT FOR FIELD ISSUE. That second line is not a chemical property. It is an order. The same bag can sit on the same shelf and become unavailable without changing a grain.","",6],["MARA","Now inspect the shipment record. Palisade bought warehouse time, transport slots, and a right to suspend release. It did not need to own every factory. It only needed to own enough of the doors between a factory and a kitchen. The system presents those doors as safety checks. Some really are. The fraud hides among the checks that were never meant to open.","",6],["ROOK","I see a failed approval. Then another. The reason is the same on every entry: THE CUSTOMER HAS NOT ACKNOWLEDGED THE UPDATED TERMS. Under customer, they have entered the name of a coastal town. Not an agency. The whole town is a customer account.","",6],["MARA","And the town never received the terms. They were sent to a terminal in this room. The contract required an answer from someone who could not enter the building. Palisade did not poison the food. It put the permission to receive the food behind a locked door, then claimed the people outside had declined delivery.","",6],["ROOK","Four-point-two seconds. That is how long I held the transfer key. The computer called the task complete. Somewhere there are people who have waited four days for a box I could open in four seconds. I do not think the progress bar was measuring the important part.","",6],["MARA","It rarely does. But keep your hand away from the delete key. If we erase this machine, we erase the receipt. We need the production history and the route history together. One proves the goods were possible. The other proves where possibility was stopped.","",6],["MARA","MSG and umami are not synonyms for the whole of each other. MSG is a seasoning that supplies glutamate. Umami is a taste. In 1913, Shintaro Kodama identified inosinate in dried bonito. In 1957, Akira Kuninaka identified guanylate as an umami substance, later associated with dried shiitake. These nucleotides can increase the umami effect of glutamate. The combined effect is called umami synergy.","S11",7],["ROOK","Two signals that do more together than alone. That is the sort of phrase our old commander would put on a recruitment poster. Then he would send one man into a room designed for six and call the missing five an efficiency gain.","",7],["MARA","In 2000, Nirupa Chaudhari, A. M. Landin, and Stephen Roper reported a taste-related variant of a glutamate receptor. Their work included a receptor cloned from rat taste buds and tested in cells. It was part of the evidence for a distinct biological basis of umami. It did not mean nobody could taste umami before 2000. Scientific recognition and everyday experience do not start on the same date.","S12",7],["MARA","In 2002, research on human T1R1 and T1R3 showed that the pair responds to glutamate, with a stronger response in the presence of certain nucleotides. That gave a molecular route for studying the synergy cooks already used. The sweet receptor uses a different pairing that includes T1R3. These are research findings about taste detection, not evidence that seasoning transmits orders.","S13",7],["ROOK","You keep stopping one step before the sinister interpretation. I appreciate the discipline. It is making this operation much harder to sell as a monster story. We have a receptor, a factory, and a bad contract. No giant machine rising out of the sea.","",7],["MARA","We do have a giant machine. You are inside its smallest office. The machine is a thousand ordinary decisions that all report to nobody. Its legs are shipping schedules. Its armor is a clause about limited liability. Its voice says the matter has been referred to another department. You cannot shoot it in the glowing weak point because the weak point is a filing system.","",7],["ROOK","Then why am I carrying a tranquilizer pistol? Was the original plan to put the paperwork to sleep? Because the paperwork has already done that to me once, during the chapter on corporate names.","",7],["MARA","The pistol is for getting out alive without adding more names to the ledger. The long explanation is for making sure you take the right ledger with you. Different tools. Try not to confuse them. We have just established that distinction as an essential scientific method.","",7],["MARA","On April 4, 1968, the New England Journal of Medicine published a letter by Robert Ho Man Kwok under the title Chinese-restaurant syndrome. The phrase is historical and stigmatizing; it is not our diagnosis. Kwok described symptoms after meals and asked about possible causes. A letter reporting a pattern is not a controlled experiment establishing a cause.","S14",8],["MARA","Historical accounts describe salt, cooking wine, and MSG among the proposed explanations. Responses and publicity helped turn an open question into a lasting association with Chinese food. The story became bigger than the evidence in the original letter. A tentative suggestion can survive in public memory after the uncertainty around it has been removed.","S15",8],["ROOK","That is the same editing mark on our briefing. The source says POSSIBLE. The summary says PROBABLE. The target sheet says CONFIRMED. Three people sign the document, and uncertainty disappears without anyone collecting another fact. By the time it reaches me, the red dot on the map looks certain enough to shoot.","",8],["MARA","The fictional program copied that exact structure. Its contractors called it confidence refinement. Every department received a shorter version. Nobody was required to read the version that still contained the doubt. Palisade could therefore claim no individual lied. Each person merely removed a word that someone above them said was unnecessary.","",8],["ROOK","I have a memory of a briefing room with no windows. They told us a warehouse held hostile material. We never opened the drums. The report said the material was neutralized. I had not thought about what that word allowed us not to see. A drum can become a threat while the people who need it disappear from the sentence.","",8],["MARA","That is why this is not a joke about a frightened diner. People can report symptoms in good faith. The failure is to turn an incomplete explanation into certainty, especially when a whole cuisine becomes the suspect. Listen to the report. Test the claim. Keep those two duties separate. Cruelty is not a method of correction.","",8],["ROOK","Put POSSIBLE back in my old report. In capital letters. Then put the missing people back on the map. I know we cannot finish either task from this room. I need an order that starts somewhere smaller than redeem my entire career.","",8],["MARA","Start by taking the unedited files. Every version, not just the final summary. The story of how a sentence changed can be as important as the sentence. We will need that chain when the contractor says the misunderstanding was ours.","",8],["MARA","The Science History Institute describes poor methods and racial prejudice in the early MSG scare. It notes how Chinese food was singled out while MSG was also used in American processed foods. That unequal suspicion is part of the ingredient's social history. Explaining it does not require us to treat every person with a question about food as dishonest or foolish.","S15",9],["ROOK","The rumor did not need a passport. It moved faster than the product. A shipment waits for a ship. A frightening sentence can cross a border between breakfast and lunch. Palisade's analysts must have loved that. They could sell an answer before anybody had finished checking the question.","",9],["MARA","In the files we recovered, the company calls that interval THE TASTE GAP. The gap is not on the tongue. It is between what a customer hears and what a customer can verify. They fund a warning, then offer a certification service, then count the new certification demand as proof that the warning was necessary. They have made a circle and printed an arrow on it.","",9],["ROOK","There is a press kit here. One page says the additive is dangerously unfamiliar. Another says their approved additive is the familiar taste of home. Same product code. Same lot number. Two photographs. In one, the bag is under a cold light. In the other, there is a grandmother holding a spoon.","",9],["MARA","The grandmother is an actor in our fictional case. The kitchen is a set. The bowl is a prop. But the hunger in the town is not a prop to the people who live there. That is the difference the contract refuses to recognize. It treats a person's need as another surface on which a message can be placed.","",9],["ROOK","This would be easier if the story ended with a secret ingredient. We could identify it, remove it, and leave. Instead you are asking me to find a lie that works even when every grain in the bag passes inspection.","",9],["MARA","Yes. And a correction that still works after we leave. A captured villain gives a speech and disappears. A false explanation can outlive the room where it was written. Our job is not complete when the transmitter goes quiet. The record has to be clear enough that the next person can check it without trusting either of us.","",9],["ROOK","You are building an operation that can survive the loss of its narrator. That is an unusually modest ambition for someone who has kept me on a radio for this long. I will take the full archive. Even the footnotes. Especially the footnotes. They seem to be where the remaining adults are hiding.","",9],["MARA","A 1995 expert assessment by the Federation of American Societies for Experimental Biology reviewed MSG safety. The FDA's account describes MSG as generally recognized as safe for use in food. It also discusses short-lived symptoms in some sensitive people after about three grams or more without food. Those conditions matter. A large isolated dose is not the same situation as a usual serving in a meal.","S16 S23",10],["MARA","Health Canada likewise discusses temporary symptoms in reports involving several grams on an empty stomach. We should not turn a safety conclusion into a promise that no person can ever react under any conditions. We should also not turn such reports into proof that ordinary use is a hidden weapon. Amount, route, food context, and the quality of the evidence belong in the same sentence.","S17",10],["ROOK","The terminal has two buttons. SAFE and UNSAFE. No field for amount. No field for conditions. No field for the person who asked the question. It is a machine that forces the operator to be more certain than the evidence. Then it saves the certainty as data.","",10],["MARA","In 2017, EFSA set a group acceptable daily intake of 30 milligrams per kilogram of body weight per day, expressed as glutamic acid, for additives E620 to E625. It also identified exposure concerns for some population groups. That is a different regulatory approach from a broad FDA summary. The group covers several glutamates, not only MSG. The number is not a line at which every meal becomes poisoning.","S18",10],["ROOK","Two agencies, different frameworks, and a contractor ready to pretend that the shorter quotation is the whole report. I know how they would use this. Put the reassuring line on the approved bag. Put the cautionary line on the competitor's bag. Leave the source off both.","",10],["MARA","We will not do that. The archive includes both. It is a history, not personal medical advice, and not a demand to eat any ingredient. People can make different food choices. What they deserve is an honest description of the choice, not a fictional mind-control claim dressed in a real chemical name.","",10],["ROOK","I am marking the SAFE button as incomplete. The system wants a reason. I will enter REQUIRES A SENTENCE. That may be the most disruptive thing I have done tonight.","",10],["MARA","Add a second reason. REQUIRES A SOURCE. Then take a copy before it asks you to acknowledge that the incomplete button is working as designed. We are nearly through the science. The remaining problem has excellent posture, a security badge, and no intention of calling itself a problem.","",10],["MARA","Glutamate supplied by MSG is chemically the same glutamate present in foods. Added MSG must be named in the ingredient list under United States rules. Other ingredients can also supply free glutamate. The absence of a separate MSG entry does not mean the complete absence of glutamate. And the similar words glutamate and gluten do not make them the same substance.","S16",11],["MARA","Health Canada's guidance discusses naturally present glutamate, added MSG, and other sources such as yeast extracts or hydrolyzed proteins. Ingredient names describe different materials and preparations. Those materials should not all be called pure MSG. A careful label reading distinguishes an ingredient from a component that several ingredients may contain.","S17",11],["ROOK","The package on my desk has a NO FEAR seal. Not a food standard. A marketing seal. Under the seal, the ingredients are printed so small I would need the security camera to read them. The system made the promise larger than the explanation.","",11],["MARA","Palisade's fictional contract goes further. It calls all unapproved distribution an unidentified nutritional event. An old woman carrying a pot to her neighbor becomes a breach in monitoring. Her soup can be perfectly ordinary. The violation is that the company did not receive the event before the neighbor received the soup.","",11],["ROOK","My mother fed the whole landing during a power cut. People brought what they had. She put the pot in the doorway because the kitchen was too small. I remember the steam on the stairwell window. Nobody signed anything. I have used more authorization codes to open this one gate than she used to feed twelve people.","",11],["MARA","Keep that memory intact. Do not let the contractor tell you it was merely an informal service failure. A label can be accurate and still omit what matters about an act. SHARED MEAL is a better description than UNREGISTERED INTAKE, even if the second phrase fits neatly in a database column.","",11],["ROOK","The dossier has a proposed upgrade. They want the bowl to carry a reader. Every serving would authenticate the person holding it. They call it frictionless dining. What happens when the network fails?","",11],["MARA","According to the contract, the provider is not liable for interruptions caused by external conditions. According to the kitchen, people remain hungry. That disagreement is the center of this operation. Not the name of the additive. The name of the person responsible for opening the door.","",11],["MARA","Ajinomoto's later history includes a frozen-food business that began in 1972. The wider group developed far beyond its original seasoning. A manufacturer's name on a bottle can therefore conceal a range of businesses and technologies. Following that development is useful, but we should not treat every product in a group as the same product simply because it has a common corporate history.","S19",12],["ROOK","We have reached the chapter where the soup company becomes several companies. I was warned that modern warfare was complicated. Nobody told me the complication would include a frozen-food division. Does this lead back to the terminal, or are we now preparing a procurement exam?","",12],["MARA","Back to the terminal. First understand the industrial logic. In our case, Palisade copied the language of diversification without doing the hard work behind it. It bought a small distributor and described itself as a nutritional systems enterprise. It rented servers and described itself as a research organization. It hired guards and described itself as a stability partner. Three new descriptions. One old warehouse.","",12],["ROOK","Ajinomoto is our real example of how a business can grow through related knowledge. Palisade is our invented example of how a business can grow through descriptions of knowledge. That difference should have been in the briefing before you gave me the waterproof explosives.","",12],["MARA","There are no explosives in your equipment. I removed them. Headquarters wanted the relay destroyed. I wanted the evidence kept. Your mission began changing before you arrived, and I did not tell you. That is not a historical fact about a manufacturer. That is a fact about me, inside this story.","",12],["ROOK","You sent me into a room with a different objective from the one my orders named. Now you are using a lecture on honest labeling to explain why. That is a bold choice of teaching method, Mara.","",12],["MARA","It is a contradiction, not a method. I need you to notice it. I could give you a clean story in which every bad decision belongs to the company and every good one belongs to us. But the archive would not support that story. I was trying to protect the files. I also took away your chance to understand the risk before you accepted it.","",12],["ROOK","Then stop making the choice for me. Tell me what the next chapter changes. All of it. Apparently we have enough time. The radio has crossed a century and the guards still have not completed a single step.","",12],["MARA","Here is the real industrial connection. Ajinomoto developed Ajinomoto Build-up Film, or ABF, an electrical insulating material used in semiconductor package substrates. The company's account traces relevant resin research to the 1970s and first adoption by a major semiconductor manufacturer to 1999. This is a connection through chemistry, materials knowledge, and industrial development. It does not mean computer chips contain table seasoning as their active ingredient.","S20",13],["MARA","Ajinomoto's account of ABF development describes a longer path through materials and resin technology, with commercial release in 1999. The resulting film belongs to electronics manufacturing. It is not edible MSG pressed into a sheet. That distinction is essential. The striking part of the history is how technical skills can move into a new industry, not a claim that a CPU runs on flavor.","S21",13],["ROOK","So a company known for a seasoning also helped build the material structure around modern processors. The machine displaying your face could sit at the end of an industrial story that began with a question about broth. That is almost too neat for this operation.","",13],["MARA","Careful. We have not inspected your actual processor's bill of materials. This is a documented industrial connection, not a verified claim about the specific computer running this game. A good twist must not become a bad hardware specification. But yes, the connection gives our fictional enemy an idea. If the same civilization depends on material supply chains for meals and information, control over access becomes valuable in both places.","",13],["ROOK","The semiconductor is not the seasoning. The company history connects them. Then our fictional contractor connects food permission to data permission. I see the shape now. They do not need to make a person into a computer. They just need to make the person's next meal depend on one.","",13],["MARA","PANTRY uses that dependency. A kitchen requests stock. A remote service scores the request. The score changes when a town misses a payment or refuses a security agreement. The service calls it demand optimization. The town calls it the third empty delivery truck this week. Both reports can describe the same event. Only one describes who waits in the rain.","",13],["ROOK","And my radio loads a voice model while the game waits. For once the waiting screen is honest. It says what is missing and lets the user choose another route. Text. A device voice. A button to leave. Palisade did not give the kitchen a Text only button.","",13],["MARA","Exactly. A fallback is a moral decision when a service becomes necessary. We built one into a long fictional call. They removed one from dinner. That is not a property of glutamate or of a semiconductor film. It is a design choice made by people who will tell us no choice was made.","",13],["MARA","The public argument did not end with early research. In 2024, an Ajinomoto-backed campaign asked the New England Journal of Medicine to address the history of the phrase used in the 1968 letter. This was also a producer participating in the public account of its product. Commercial interest does not by itself make a claim false. It does make source identity relevant when we judge the claim.","S22",14],["ROOK","Everyone wants to own the explanation. The company. The critic. The ministry. The man who writes the mission title. I suppose that includes us. We have renamed a whole military operation after a food additive, then asked the player to trust the people talking over the gunfire.","",14],["MARA","Which is why the source archive stays outside our authority. You can open it. Follow the dates. Read the actual assessments. Notice where an industry source ends and our invention starts. Our history has a research cutoff in September 2026. Everything in the mission's year, 2037, is an imagined continuation, not a report from the future. No narrator gets a permanent exemption from being checked.","",14],["ROOK","That is a lot of trust to place in a source button. People click the glowing thing. They do not always read the small thing under it. I have spent most of my career being the person who follows the glowing thing.","",14],["MARA","Then tonight we make the small thing harder to lose. Each historical passage keeps its source number. Each invented part calls itself fiction. The truth is not that every fear was stupid or every corporate claim was pure. The truth is a sequence of observations, technologies, tests, interests, and people. It does not fit on a single red warning label.","",14],["ROOK","And the whole history is not a single final report. New work can change parts of it. A source can have a limitation. A date can refer to more than one event. You are turning certainty into an obstacle course.","",14],["MARA","No. I am removing the false shortcut. Certainty is useful when it is earned. Palisade's system sells it before the work is done. That is the product we are here to disable. The MSG can remain on the shelf. Nobody needs to destroy a seasoning to stop a lie about it.","",14],["ROOK","Then our objective is finally clear. Not stop the taste. Stop the toll. It is less impressive on a recruitment poster. It is a better reason to leave this room alive.","",14],["MARA","Now we leave documented history and enter the fiction in the recovered file. Project PANTRY stands for Population Allocation, Nutrition Tracking, and Ration Yield. The expansion was written after the name. You can tell because every engineer in the minutes uses a different word for the final letter. A committee spent six weeks naming the system and eleven minutes discussing the people it could exclude.","",15],["ROOK","The oldest document says the goal was to reduce waste. That does not sound like an evil plan. My unit threw away more food than we admitted. Some of it never left the truck. A system that stopped that would have been useful.","",15],["MARA","The first goal was useful. The next contract added identity checks. Then debt scoring. Then security conditions. Each addition arrived as a small update. Nobody held a meeting called SHOULD HUNGER BECOME A PUNISHMENT. They held meetings called VERSION REVIEW. The punishment appeared between two revisions of a form.","",15],["ROOK","Here is the master table. The column says ENHANCEMENT. I thought it meant flavor enhancement. It means a surcharge for access. The food gets more expensive when the town has fewer alternatives. The software has defined need as a premium feature.","",15],["MARA","Their internal joke is Monosodium Governance. It is a pun, not a new chemical. They knew a seasoning was a poor villain. They made it the mascot anyway. A bag of crystals looks simple. Nobody expects the contract behind it to contain a model of an entire population. The ordinary object kept the extraordinary demand out of view.","",15],["ROOK","Then why keep the complete history on this terminal? Why attach an honest account to a dishonest service? A villain with a tidy filing system should at least know which drawer makes him look bad.","",15],["MARA","An engineer copied it here. Someone wanted a later reader to see what the company had borrowed and what it had invented. The source archive is the part they could not make proprietary. PANTRY tried to turn a long public history into its own private origin story. The engineer left the door open between the two.","",15],["ROOK","The engineer signed with a kitchen shift number. Table Four. Not a name. You told me to remember the bowl. We are back at the bowl, aren't we? We have gone through factories, receptors, and semiconductor film to reach an object I could have picked up at the start.","",15],["MARA","Table Four was my mother's station. Not her employee number. The fourth table in a temporary kitchen. She used it to sort deliveries. The table had one short leg, and she put folded cardboard under it. The same cardboard stayed there for three winters because every inspection listed the table as stable.","",16],["ROOK","Your mother was the engineer?","",16],["MARA","No. My mother was the cook. I was the engineer. I wrote PANTRY's first allocation model. It assigned stock according to the number of meals a kitchen expected to serve. When there was not enough, it was supposed to make the shortage visible. I believed that a precise record would force somebody to correct it. I did not consider how useful a precise record could be to someone who wanted to choose the shortage.","",16],["ROOK","What changed?","",16],["MARA","One line. The model originally asked how much each kitchen needed. A later build asked how much each kitchen was permitted to receive. I approved the update because the interface looked the same. Same blue bars. Same reassuring total. The developer note said it aligned the tool with the current contract. I read that sentence and did not ask to see the contract.","",16],["ROOK","Table Four was excluded.","",16],["MARA","For missing identity records. My mother fed people who had lost their papers. The system saw meals without approved recipients. It called them inventory leakage. A manager proposed closing the kitchen to protect the integrity of the data. I tried to correct the records. My mother asked why I was trying so hard to prove that a person existed after the person had already arrived hungry.","",16],["ROOK","She was right.","",16],["MARA","Yes. That is the part I cannot improve with an explanation. She was right, and I still spent the next week building a better exception form. By the time I understood that the exception was the purpose, the contract had been renewed. The kitchen reopened only after the town accepted a security provider. Palisade invoiced the reopened door as a successful intervention.","",16],["ROOK","Did your mother know you wrote it?","",16],["MARA","She knew. She kept my place at the table. That was worse than a speech. She did not reduce me to my worst decision, so I could not use her anger as proof that I was beyond repair. I had to sit down, eat the meal, and decide what to do after it. The bowl beside you is hers. I sent it with the engineer who copied the archive. I needed one object in that room to keep its original purpose.","",16],["ROOK","My unit guarded a depot called Haven. They told us the local council had stolen relief stock. Every night people gathered at the gate. We treated the crowd as a security problem. At dawn, the trucks left under escort. We were congratulated for restoring the distribution network. Now I am looking at Haven in the ledger. The stock was never missing.","",17],["MARA","It was on hold. The council refused a payment clause. The depot had enough for the scheduled kitchens, but the authorization remained red. The crowd you guarded against included the people who were supposed to receive it. Their presence was entered as a reason to delay release. The delay produced the crowd, and the crowd justified the delay.","",17],["ROOK","My commander said the situation would stabilize when the civilians learned to follow procedure. I repeated that sentence. I remember the exact sound of my voice. Calm. Professional. As though being calm made the sentence less ugly. Then I went inside and ate a hot meal from the same stock.","",17],["MARA","The contractor used your unit's incident reports as proof of instability. Then it used the instability score to obtain a longer contract. I found your signature on three reports. I selected you for this mission because you could recognize the place. I should have told you that before you got on the boat.","",17],["ROOK","You used my record as a key. Not my skill. Not just my skill. You thought guilt would open a door that orders could not.","",17],["MARA","I thought recognition might. I also knew you had a right to refuse. I did not give you the facts needed to exercise that right. The company is not the only party in this story that has confused a useful outcome with permission. I cannot fix that by changing the name of the operation again.","",17],["ROOK","Then here is my decision, with the facts finally attached. I will take the records. I will get them out. Not to erase my signature. To put it where it belongs, beside the orders and the people they affected. Do not cut my pages from the archive to make the leak easier to defend.","",17],["MARA","I will not. There is another message in the final directory. Your old commander wants the original mission completed. Destroy the relay. Destroy the source. He calls the archived history irrelevant background. He says a field agent should not have to read it.","",17],["ROOK","For the first time tonight, I disagree with the man who wants a shorter call. Keep the channel open. We have reached the part where the length is evidence. If the story had stopped at MSG IS THE THREAT, I would have destroyed the wrong thing and called it a clean operation.","",17],["MARA","Your transfer did two things. It copied the evidence and uploaded a signed release to the local store. The release removes Palisade's artificial hold from the cargo at this station. It does not rewrite every supply system in the world. It does not make the sea calm. It opens one door and preserves the record of who kept it shut.","",18],["ROOK","So the progress bar actually had two jobs, neither of which it explained. I am adding a third reason to that incomplete interface report. REQUIRES A VERB. Download what. Upload what. For whom. I would like one screen in this building to answer those questions before I press its largest button.","",18],["MARA","The release has been acknowledged. The kitchen network will receive the manifests. The source files are on your field unit. You can finish this call, close it, or return to it from the relay archive. Closing the call will not cancel the transfer. You do not have to sit through my entire confession to complete the mission.","",18],["ROOK","We have crossed that threshold already. At this point, leaving early would feel like getting off a train after carrying it over the mountain. Give me the last instruction. An actual instruction this time. Something I can do with my hands and feet.","",18],["MARA","Return to the southeast dock. Lose the guards before you board. Take the field unit. Leave the food intact. On your way out, put the photograph in the office upright. Do not take the bowl. The next shift needs something to eat from, not another empty space that proves a soldier was here.","",18],["ROOK","And the real manufacturer? The scientists? The people whose history we used to find this invented crime?","",18],["MARA","Leave their names attached to what they actually did. The 1866 chemical work. Ikeda's 1908 taste research. The 1909 seasoning. The factories and the fermentation breakthrough. The later taste studies, safety assessments, and industrial materials. Do not borrow their authority for our fiction, and do not give them our fictional guilt. A source is not a costume for a plot twist.","",18],["ROOK","Understood. The additive was never the enemy. The receipt was the map. The closed door was the weapon. And a very long radio call was apparently the only available transport between those three facts.","",18],["MARA","One more thing, Rook.","",19],["ROOK","No. Those words are how a five-minute briefing becomes a family history with a semiconductor appendix. We have done the nineteenth century. We have named the bacterium. We have discussed two taste receptors and a shipping contract. Somewhere outside this room, a snowflake has applied for a pension while waiting for me to move.","",19],["MARA","The archive needs a title. Not PANTRY. Not Monosodium Governance. Those were their names. What do you want the public copy to say?","",19],["ROOK","MSG. The ordinary name. Then a subtitle that tells the truth. The Long Aftertaste. Do not put SECRET in front of it. Do not put FORBIDDEN in front of it. If the facts can stand up, they can stand up without a man whispering that the world does not want you to know.","",19],["MARA","The Long Aftertaste. File title set. Source notes preserved. Fiction marked. You are free to end the call.","",19],["ROOK","Before I do, there is something I need to ask. When you said the mission clock was paused, did that include the guard outside the door? Because I have learned enough history to earn a degree and he is still in the middle of the same footstep. I am beginning to suspect the most powerful device on this station is the conversation system.","",19],["MARA","It is. It can stop an armed patrol until two people finish listening. It can give a frightened operative enough time to ask what a word means. It can let a player leave and return without punishment. Those are not realistic military capabilities. They are choices made for this game. We may as well use them for something better than another order to destroy a transmitter.","",19],["ROOK","Then let the guards walk again. Let the snow fall. I will cross the dock, board the boat, and carry the whole inconvenient file home. Not because every page agrees. Because the pages that disagree are the reason the file matters.","",19],["MARA","Good. And Rook? The photograph.","",19],["ROOK","I remember. A bowl is for food. A photograph is for a person. A history is for checking. And a radio call, against all available evidence, is supposed to end. Rook out.","",19]],"sources":{"S01":{"title":"Umami Information Center · What is umami?","url":"https://www.umamiinfo.com/what/whatisumami/","note":"Food traditions and naturally occurring glutamate. Industry-supported education."},"S02":{"title":"Ajinomoto · Encyclopedia of Amino Acids","url":"https://www.ajinomoto.co.jp/company/en/amino/manabou/about.html","note":"Ritthausen and wheat gluten, 1866. Manufacturer science history."},"S03":{"title":"Ajinomoto · The discovery of umami","url":"https://www.ajinomoto.com/umami/discovery-of-umami","note":"Ikeda and kombu, 1908. The producer describes its own history."},"S04":{"title":"Kikunae Ikeda · New Seasonings (1909; translated 2002)","url":"https://www.srut.org/english/info-en/ikeda/","note":"Original paper, later English translation in Chemical Senses. Primary research."},"S05":{"title":"Ajinomoto Group · History","url":"https://www.ajinomoto.com/aboutus/history","note":"Suzuki, the 1909 product launch, and the company origins. Producer history."},"S06":{"title":"Chiaki Sano · History of glutamate production (2009)","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19640955/","note":"Review of production methods. Author affiliated with Ajinomoto."},"S07":{"title":"Ajinomoto Group · Corporate timeline","url":"https://www.ajinomoto.com/aboutus/history/ajinomoto-group-history","note":"Factories, overseas offices, names, and dates. Producer history."},"S08":{"title":"Kyowa Kirin · History","url":"https://www.kyowakirin.com/history/index.html","note":"Kyowa Hakko and glutamic-acid fermentation in 1956. Producer history."},"S09":{"title":"Shin-ichi Hashimoto · Discovery and History of Amino Acid Fermentation (2017)","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27909736/","note":"Corynebacterium glutamicum and industrial fermentation. Research history."},"S10":{"title":"Ajinomoto · What is MSG and how is it made?","url":"https://www.ajinomoto.com/msg/what-is-msg-and-how-is-it-made","note":"Sugar feedstocks, fermentation, purification, and crystallization. Producer process account."},"S11":{"title":"Umami Information Center · Umami research timeline","url":"https://www.umamiinfo.com/what/whatisumami/","note":"Kodama, Kuninaka, inosinate, and guanylate. Industry-supported education."},"S12":{"title":"Chaudhari, Landin and Roper · A metabotropic glutamate receptor variant functions as a taste receptor (2000)","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10649565/","note":"Original receptor research. Rat taste cells; not proof of a human mind-control effect."},"S13":{"title":"Li and colleagues · Human receptors for sweet and umami taste (2002)","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11917125/","note":"Original T1R1/T1R3 receptor research."},"S14":{"title":"Robert Ho Man Kwok · 1968 NEJM correspondence","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25276867/","note":"Bibliographic record of the 4 April 1968 letter. Its historical title is quoted in context."},"S15":{"title":"Science History Institute · The Rotten Science Behind the MSG Scare (2023)","url":"https://www.sciencehistory.org/stories/magazine/the-rotten-science-behind-the-msg-scare/","note":"Historical account of the letter, stigma, and later disputed claims."},"S16":{"title":"U.S. FDA · Questions and Answers on MSG","url":"https://www.fda.gov/food/food-additives-petitions/questions-and-answers-monosodium-glutamate-msg","note":"U.S. safety assessment, FASEB conclusions, dose context, and labeling. Regulator."},"S17":{"title":"Health Canada · MSG and other sources of glutamate","url":"https://www.canada.ca/en/health-canada/services/food-nutrition/food-safety/food-additives/monosodium-glutamate-questions-answers.html","note":"Dose context and Canadian labeling. Regulator."},"S18":{"title":"EFSA · Re-evaluation of glutamates added to food (2017)","url":"https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/press/news/170712","note":"Group ADI of 30 mg/kg body weight/day, expressed as glutamic acid. Regulator."},"S19":{"title":"Ajinomoto Frozen Foods Europe · Our history","url":"https://www.ajinomoto-frozenfoods.eu/en/our-history/","note":"1909 name and 1972 frozen-food expansion. Producer history."},"S20":{"title":"Ajinomoto · Build-up Film","url":"https://www.ajinomoto.com/innovation/our_innovation/buildupfilm","note":"ABF and semiconductor package insulation. Manufacturer technical account."},"S21":{"title":"Ajinomoto · Its role in semiconductor manufacturing","url":"https://www.ajinomoto.com/stories/the-ajinomoto-groups-unexpected-role-in-semiconductor-manufacturing-the-insulating-film-abf-born-from-aminoscience","note":"Materials research and the 1999 ABF milestone. Manufacturer interview."},"S22":{"title":"Food & Wine · The Know MSG campaign (23 September 2024)","url":"https://www.foodandwine.com/ajinomoto-know-msg-campaign-8715564","note":"Interview on a 2024 campaign. Commercial participation is stated in the dialogue."},"S23":{"title":"Walker and Lupien · The Safety Evaluation of MSG (2000)","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S002231662214037X","note":"Dates the FASEB report to July 1995. Review of regulatory assessments."}},"words":8214,"researchDate":"7 September 2026"};
